---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import { ADDRESS_ONE_LINE, COMPANY, CONTACT_LINKS } from '../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Nirvigna collects and uses personal data from this website and the contact form, under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023."
  lastUpdated="8 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    This notice explains what personal data {COMPANY.legalName} (“{COMPANY.brand}”, “we”, “us”) collects through this website,
    why, and the choices and rights you have under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (the “DPDP Act”) and the rules
    made under it.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    {COMPANY.legalName} (CIN {COMPANY.cin}) is the Data Fiduciary for personal data collected through this website. Registered
    office: {ADDRESS_ONE_LINE}. Email: <a href={CONTACT_LINKS.email}>{COMPANY.email}</a>. Phone: {COMPANY.phoneDisplay}.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect and why</h2>
  <h3>2.1 The contact form</h3>
  <p>When you use the contact form, we receive:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, business name, phone number and email address;</li>
    <li>your type of business and your message;</li>
    <li>your consent to this notice; and</li>
    <li>a hidden spam-check field, which should be empty when a person fills in the form.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this only to reply to your enquiry, arrange a demo if you ask for one, and keep a record of the conversation. We
    process it on the basis of the consent you give by ticking the consent box. The website itself does not store what you send;
    it goes straight to our form service.
  </p>

  <h3>2.2 Email, phone and WhatsApp</h3>
  <p>
    If you email, call or message us, we receive your contact details and whatever you choose to tell us, and use them to reply.
  </p>

  <h3>2.3 WhatsApp links go to Meta</h3>
  <p>
    The WhatsApp links on this website open WhatsApp, a service run by Meta. When you use them, Meta receives information about
    you under its own terms and privacy policy, which we do not control. If you prefer not to use WhatsApp, please email or call
    us instead.
  </p>

  <h3>2.4 Visiting the website</h3>
  <p>
    This website does not use cookies, analytics, advertising trackers or third-party scripts, and its fonts are served from our
    own site. Nothing is stored in your browser by us.
  </p>
  <p>
    When the website is published, it is intended to be served through a content delivery network (Amazon CloudFront). Its
    access logs may record your IP address, the date and time, the page requested, the referring page and your browser’s user
    agent. We will use these logs only to keep the website secure and running, and will keep them for
    <Placeholder text="[PLACEHOLDER: log retention period]" />.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Who we share it with</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Service providers who process data for us — for example our email provider, our form service and our hosting provider —
      only for the purposes above: <Placeholder text="[PLACEHOLDER: list of processors]" />.
    </li>
    <li>A qualified CA/CS, only where you engage us for work that needs one and agree to it.</li>
    <li>Government authorities or courts, where the law requires us to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal data, and we do not use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>4. Where it is stored</h2>
  <p><Placeholder text="[PLACEHOLDER: storage location of form submissions and email — to be confirmed before launch]" /></p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiry data only as long as needed for the purpose it was collected for, or as the law requires:
    <Placeholder text="[PLACEHOLDER: retention period for enquiries]" />. We erase it when you withdraw consent, unless the law
    requires us to keep it.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the DPDP Act you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>withdraw your consent at any time, as easily as you gave it;</li>
    <li>ask for a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how we use it;</li>
    <li>ask us to correct, complete, update or erase your personal data;</li>
    <li>have your grievances addressed by us; and</li>
    <li>nominate another person to exercise these rights if you die or become unable to.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use any of these rights, write to <a href={CONTACT_LINKS.email}>{COMPANY.email}</a> or see our
    <a href="/grievance/">grievance contact</a>. We may need to confirm your identity before acting on a request.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    Please contact our <a href="/grievance/">Grievance Officer</a> first. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may
    complain to the Data Protection Board of India.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable security safeguards to protect personal data against breaches, and will notify you and the Data Protection Board of India of a breach as the law requires.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>This website is meant for adults running or starting businesses. We do not knowingly collect personal data of children.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>We will post any changes on this page with a new date.</p>
</LegalLayout>
